# 0031 XeMTL plugin: compressed scanout images, IOSurface import by surface, image arena, census and compile statistics
#
# Base:  plugin/ after 0005 + 0006 + 0007 + 0026 (XeGfx 0.0.35 · 497d521e)
# Files: plugin/{NVMTLEventSync.m, NVMTLObjects.h, NVMTLObjects.m, XeMTLDevice.m, nvmtl_vk.c, nvmtl_vk.h}
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0031-plugin-ccs-scanout-surface-import-arena.patch
# Build: XeMTLDriver 19bea7235828 after ad-hoc signing (needs core 0028, accel 0029, libdrm 0032)
#
# Compressed scanout (docs/render-compression.md):
#   - a scanout surface that has a private copy (page-off, 0026) is drawn into a Tile4 + MTL RC CCS image instead, and
#     the display scans that image itself, when the accel reports compressed scanout on (selector 2, flag 0x4).  The
#     image has no fast-cleared blocks: MTL_RC_CCS has no clear colour for the display to resolve.
#   - the image's memory is exported, its GEM handle found again in WindowServer's DRM file (drmPrimeFDToHandle) and
#     pinned with the core's BO_SCANOUT; the core's reply size is checked against the image's memory (a stale export
#     once named a surface import of a different size), then the image is registered with selector 9 (surface ID,
#     token, main pitch, CCS offset and pitch) and dropped with selector 10.
#   - a scanout surface is promoted while both compressed scanout and page-off are on; a compressed image goes back to
#     drawing over the surface's pages when compressed scanout is switched off or 0026's page-off rules mark the
#     surface for demotion.
#
# Import by surface: before ANV imports an IOSurface WindowServer draws from (a host-pointer import), the plugin asks
# the accel for a ticket (selector 11) and announces it with the pointer and size (the core's SURF_EXPECT, on ANV's
# DRM file); the import that follows is then made of the surface's own memory (0028).  Counters for announced and
# refused imports are in the plugin log.
#
# Image arena: device images up to 8 MiB are suballocated from 64 MiB VkDeviceMemory blocks instead of one allocation
# each (fewer GEM objects for the kernel to look up and pin on every execbuffer).  Off with XEMTL_NO_ARENA=1 or
# /Library/GPUBundles/.xemtl-no-arena.
#
# Explicit residency: when ANV exports anv_xemtl_* (0033) and /Library/GPUBundles/.xemtl-no-xres is absent, imported
# surface memory is marked explicit and each submitted part declares the imports its textures use, so the other
# imports stay out of that execbuffer.  The published setup keeps it held off (the file exists).
#
# Diagnostics (all off unless asked for):
#   - texture census: /tmp/nvmtl-texcensus-request writes /private/tmp/xemtl-texcensus.txt: images of 1024x600 or
#     more by the path that made them (plain, heap, buffer, pages, pages-t4, pageoff, copied, vram, ccs) and size, and
#     the passes drawn into them with their GPU time while passtime is armed.
#   - compile statistics: XEMTL_PSTAT=1 or /private/tmp/xemtl-pstat-on at process start logs ANV's statistics for every
#     fragment executable (instructions, SENDs, cycles, spills, SIMD width) and keeps each pipeline's SPIR-V in
#     /private/tmp/xemtl-pstat (WindowServer's home is not writable); ptpso lines carry the fragment function's
#     constants, which select Core Animation's shader variant.
#   - per-draw GPU time: /tmp/nvmtl-drawtime-request together with passtime adds one timestamp per draw (shader, vertex
#     count, scissor, first two textures).  It serialises the draws, so absolute times are too large.
#
